---
// Front 120 — bpp islands · examples/src/app/product/[id]/page.bpp
//
// Demonstrates: step 4 in a `.bpp` page — a server island. The page is the same
// for every visitor, so it is prerendered; the avatar depends on the visitor's
// session, so it is NOT in the page. `server:defer` leaves the fallback in the
// markup and the browser fetches the component from its own endpoint.
//
//   <Avatar server:defer>
//     <GenericAvatar slot="fallback" />
//   </Avatar>
//
// The page reads nothing from the request — `cookies()` is called inside
// `Avatar`, in the ISLAND's request — so the page reaches no `#[serverOnly]`
// hook and `#[page]` prerenders it at comptime (decision 202).
//
// `Avatar` is a `.bp` module: `#[deferred]` is a decorator on its function (see
// `src/app/page.bpp` of this tree for why). `GenericAvatar` needs none, and is a
// `.bpp` component.
//
// The `.bp` form of this page, with its tests: `page` in
// `server-island-example.bp` at the root of `examples/`.
//
// Upstream: astro-docs/22-server-islands.md
//           https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/server-islands/

import {h1} from "jhonstart";
import {components.Avatar};
import {components.GenericAvatar};

val id = params.id;
---
<h1>Product {id}</h1>
<Avatar size={48} server:defer>
  <GenericAvatar size={48} slot="fallback" />
</Avatar>
